{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"120a4c1eb0ef646d","name":"card_event_attack_in_the_colonies","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Italy/events/card_event_attack_in_the_colonies","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ATTACK IN THE COLONIES","text":"Deal 3 damage to an enemy. Your HQ gains +5 defense.","flavorText":"Following the footsteps of their German ally, Italy declared war on Britain in June 1940. Their goal was to occupy British and French colonies in Africa as well as seizing control of the Suez Canal from the British. Initially the Italian forces managed to seize control of the upper Nile Valley in Sudan and British Somaliland. More troops were sent to capture the Northern part of the British colony of Kenya and to advance into Egypt in the hopes of reaching the Suez Canal. However, by this time the British managed to execute three counter offensives, and with great help from the RAF they managed to push back the Italians. What followed was a series of battles for control of Libya and regions of Egypt, and despite being reinforced by the Germans, the last Italian troops in East Africa were defeated at the Battle of Gondar in November 1941. However, several thousand Italian troops continued to wage a guerrilla war until September 1943, when Italy surrendered to the Allies.","faction":"Italy","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_attack_in_the_colonies","title":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_attack_in_the_colonies_title","SourceString":"ATTACK IN THE COLONIES","LocalizedString":"ATTACK IN THE COLONIES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Italy","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_attack_in_the_colonies_text","SourceString":"Deal 3 damage to an enemy. Your HQ gains +5 defense.","LocalizedString":"Deal 3 damage to an enemy. Your HQ gains +5 defense."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_attack_in_the_colonies_history","SourceString":"Following the footsteps of their German ally, Italy declared war on Britain in June 1940. Their goal was to occupy British and French colonies in Africa as well as seizing control of the Suez Canal from the British. Initially the Italian forces managed to seize control of the upper Nile Valley in Sudan and British Somaliland. More troops were sent to capture the Northern part of the British colony of Kenya and to advance into Egypt in the hopes of reaching the Suez Canal. However, by this time the British managed to execute three counter offensives, and with great help from the RAF they managed to push back the Italians. What followed was a series of battles for control of Libya and regions of Egypt, and despite being reinforced by the Germans, the last Italian troops in East Africa were defeated at the Battle of Gondar in November 1941. However, several thousand Italian troops continued to wage a guerrilla war until September 1943, when Italy surrendered to the Allies.","LocalizedString":"Following the footsteps of their German ally, Italy declared war on Britain in June 1940. Their goal was to occupy British and French colonies in Africa as well as seizing control of the Suez Canal from the British. Initially the Italian forces managed to seize control of the upper Nile Valley in Sudan and British Somaliland. More troops were sent to capture the Northern part of the British colony of Kenya and to advance into Egypt in the hopes of reaching the Suez Canal. However, by this time the British managed to execute three counter offensives, and with great help from the RAF they managed to push back the Italians. What followed was a series of battles for control of Libya and regions of Egypt, and despite being reinforced by the Germans, the last Italian troops in East Africa were defeated at the Battle of Gondar in November 1941. However, several thousand Italian troops continued to wage a guerrilla war until September 1943, when Italy surrendered to the Allies."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isInPermanentPool":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Cues/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Italy/t_airstrike.t_airstrike","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/ATTACK_IN_THE_COLONIES.ATTACK_IN_THE_COLONIES","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":375.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_attack_in_the_colonies_photo","SourceString":"Italian infantry in front of a captured outpost in British Somaliland, 1940.","LocalizedString":"Italian infantry in front of a captured outpost in British Somaliland, 1940."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"isDirectDamage":true},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_attack_in_the_colonies_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_GetOppositeSide_oppositeSide","type":"ESideEnum","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_EqualEqual_ByteByte_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"body":[{"op":"Context","at":0,"object":{"op":